(Here’s the hard truth: the real game isn’t about balancing between Enterprise and SMB; it’s about rethinking) Tj
T* (your position in the market entirely. Right now, with Enterprise inquiries, you’re just fishing in a well-saturated) Tj
T* (pond, trying to differentiate your offerings in a crowded space. Meanwhile, SMBs represent not just a revenue) Tj
T* (stream but an opportunity to fundamentally disrupt your competitive landscape. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (My advice? Don’t just dip your toes into SMB features—make a significant bet on it. Think about the value you) Tj
T* (could unlock by creating a flexible, scalable platform that SMBs can’t resist. The question you should be asking) Tj
T* (is: what innovation can we launch that shifts the narrative? You're not merely adding features; you're building a) Tj
T* (movement.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Invest in a talent acquisition strategy that prioritizes customer empathy and agile execution to meet SMB needs.) Tj
T* (This is a risk—yes, it may require resources upfront—but in five years, it could change your company's trajectory) Tj
T* (entirely. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (So, go out and hire a dedicated SMB team. Make your bet.) Tj
