(Let’s address the heart of the problem framing here. The PM presents a tension between Enterprise and SMB) Tj
T* (strategies, under the illusion that revenue saturation in Enterprise necessitates a shift focus. However, the) Tj
T* (hidden assumption is that we are only as good as our current inbound requests and existing features. What if we) Tj
T* (reframed success not merely around existing revenue lines but around what untapped value we could unlock? ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Sticking solely to Enterprise could yield higher margins if we pivot our approach to deliver significantly more) Tj
T* (value, rather than diluting our efforts and resources by venturing into the SMB space. As seen when I discussed) Tj
T* (changing metrics dramatically to derive insights, what if we shifted our focus from the number of inbound) Tj
T* (requests to the depth of relationships and expansion within current Enterprise clients?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (We should not rush to add features for SMBs. Instead, let’s consider this: How can we scale our existing) Tj
T* (Enterprise relationships, perhaps even generating more value through higher-tier, more customized offerings? ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (So, the reframed problem statement is: "How can we enhance and deepen our relationships with existing) Tj
T* (Enterprise clients to unlock new revenue streams, rather than diversifying into SMBs?") Tj
